$ enola coverage .
exit: 0
--- stdout
No services in this graph, so there are no cross-repo edges to report on.

Coverage compares repositories against each other, so it needs at least two loaded
in one graph. Index a cluster and re-run:

    enola --generate ci/cluster.yaml   # a config listing several repos under `repos:`
    enola coverage ci/cluster.yaml
--- stderr
enola: no mcp-arch.yaml in <TMP>/go_sample, using built-in defaults
enola coverage: repo <TMP>/go_sample (built-in default config)
